course: dictionary
lesson: 13864
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Her anger was justified, because someone had broken her bike.» Here justified means fair, with a good reason.
explain: Justify means to give a good reason for something. «She justified her answer by showing each step of her sums.» Justified is the past form of justify, so it means she gave a good reason.
explain: In a book or on a computer, justified can describe the lines of text. «The text is justified» means every line starts and ends at the same straight edge on the page. Ask yourself: is this about feelings, reasons, or the shape of the lines?
fact: Justified is an adjective when it means fair or having a good reason.
fact: «Justified» (text) means lined up so that both the left and right edges are straight.
fact: Justify is a verb, meaning to give a good reason for something; justified is its past form.
fact: Phrases to know: «feel justified» means you feel you have a good reason; «fully justified» means completely fair.
exercise: «Her anger was justified, because someone had broken her window.» What does justified mean? | Angry for no reason at all | Cheerful and calm | *Fair, with a good reason | Hidden under a bed
exercise: «She justified her answer by showing each step of her sums.» What did she do? | Forgot her answer | Shouted her answer loudly | Changed her answer to a new one | *Gave a good reason for her answer
exercise: In a printed book, what does «justified text» look like? | Only the left edge is neat | Written only in capital letters | *Both the left and right edges are straight | Each line is a different colour
test: «The team felt justified in asking for a rest after the long match.» What does justified mean here? | Won the match | Lost all their energy | Very tired and cross | *Had a good reason
test: Mia's teacher says, «Please justify your answer with a reason.» What should Mia do? | *Give a reason why her answer is right | Ask someone else to write it for her | Rub the answer out | Shout the answer across the room
exam: «The printed notes are justified, so every line starts and ends at the same straight edge.» What does justified mean in this sentence? | Fair and reasonable | *Lined up so both edges are straight | Written in pencil | Very old
